## Phase 5 — HR Agent: COMPLETE (5/5 tests passing)

**Location:** `/workspace/projects/sanad_agent/hr_agent/`

### What was built

A FastAPI service (port 8200) that gives the Orchestrator the ability to provision and retire agent containers on demand.

**Four endpoints:**

| Endpoint | What it does |
|---|---|
| `POST /agents/recruit` | git clone → docker build → docker run → health-check (12×5s) → register with Orchestrator |
| `POST /agents/validate/{agent_id}` | GET /health on the container, confirm ONLINE with Orchestrator |
| `DELETE /agents/{agent_id}` | Blue/green: check not BUSY → docker stop/rm → PATCH OFFLINE |
| `GET /health` | Liveness check; verifies Docker socket is reachable |

**Key design decisions:**
- `docker_client.py` wraps the Python Docker SDK — no subprocess for Docker ops
- Blocking Docker calls (`build`, `run`, `stop`, `rm`) are dispatched via `asyncio.to_thread()` so the async FastAPI event loop is never blocked
- Health-check is natively async (`httpx.AsyncClient` + `asyncio.sleep`)
- On health-check failure: full cleanup (stop container, rm container, rm image) before returning 500
- Orchestrator registration failure is non-fatal — agent stays running with a locally-generated ID
- `_agent_registry` in-memory dict tracks container metadata; Orchestrator is the authoritative registry

